{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrictComplementarityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrictComplementarityPair","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L97-L107","doc":"**Trivial strict-complementarity pair** for the constraint-\nfree case with PSD cost.  The active set is empty (no constraints\nto be active), so `active_dual_pos` and `inactive_dual_zero` both\nhold vacuously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.hasStrongDuality_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.hasStrongDuality_empty","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L89-L95","doc":"**Strong duality for the constraint-free case with PSD cost.**\n(Formerly an unconditional global instance; see\n`trivialStrongDualityPair` for why the PSD-cost hypothesis is needed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrongDualityPair","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L71-L87","doc":"**Strong-duality pair for the constraint-free case, given a PSD cost.**\n\nPrimal point `0`, empty dual point.  Dual feasibility is exactly\n`cost ⪰ 0` (the dual slack *is* the cost), and both objectives are `0`.\n\nThe hypothesis is necessary, not a convenience.  This used to be stated\nfor every cost, which type-checked only because `dual_feas` and `obj_eq`\nwere `True`.  For a cost with a negative direction `v` (e.g. `T = -1`,\n`n = 1`) the primal objective `tr(T Φ)` is unbounded below on `Φ ⪰ 0`\n(take `Φ = t · v vᴴ`, `t → ∞`), so there is no optimal pair at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.dualObjAt_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.dualObjAt_empty","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L66-L69","doc":"With no constraints the dual objective is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.dualSlack_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.dualSlack_empty","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L61-L64","doc":"With no constraints the dual slack is the cost itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.one_isStrictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.one_isStrictlyFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L54-L59","doc":"The identity matrix is strictly feasible for any constraint-free\nSDP (positive-definite, no constraints to satisfy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.zero_isFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.zero_isFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L48-L52","doc":"For any `SDPPrimal n R Empty`, the zero matrix is feasible\n(vacuously satisfies all constraints). ","signatureChunk":0}]}